        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the answer is <strong class="text-white">$900 to $1,500</strong> — enough
            for frame stability, the right deck length, a fold that works and a real warranty, and
            not so much that you are buying durability you will never consume.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Answer the walk-or-run question honestly, count the
            <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">subscription</a>
            before comparing anything, and reserve $80 for a mat and lubricant. Those cost less
            than the last $300 of treadmill and matter considerably more.
          </p>
